      "writtenOn": "2022-12-27T09:17:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This disagrees with a constraint that you you built into SyncSM. At the very least, it breaks a degree of freedom ; at worst it doesn\u0027t work.\n\nSyncSM can be created either on the current thread, or on a thread that\u0027s not started yet. But IIRC `Handler.getLooper()` returns null if the thread is not started yet (because you can\u0027t make a `Looper` except by calling `prepare()`, which uses the current thread). That means this code forbids the second way of creating the sync SM.\n\nSo if it\u0027s impossible to pass a looper for a thread that\u0027s not started yet, that means this constructor must run on the same thread that\u0027s passed. So that means this must run on the thread of the passed handler, or it will throw.\n\nConsidering you\u0027ll want to use this shim for both the state machines in tethering, I think you do need to have both styles possible (or you wouldn\u0027t have created both styles in SyncSM – if you don\u0027t need both of them, then we should go back and remove the one you don\u0027t need).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 41,
        "startChar": 49,
        "endLine": 41,
        "endChar": 80
      },
      "revId": "c0e330450df1335090ce45b35b44054f4a7540dc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "20e19546_d4684223",
