      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-27T09:17:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How necessary is this ? The new state machine doesn\u0027t have any requirement to run on a Handler thread. I get that for the time being you\u0027ll use one, and that\u0027s fine, but really :\n- For async state machine it would be a lot less confusing if it was not possible to grab the handler out of the SM and do things with it\n- For sync state machine it would be much better if we didn\u0027t impose a Handler since sync SM has no requirement for it\n\nWhere are you going to use this ? If you can remove this immediately, then please remove it. If you can\u0027t then at least please add a TODO to remove it.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 50,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 50,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "c0e330450df1335090ce45b35b44054f4a7540dc",
